      en: "Morocco is a country of convergence: its identity, one and indivisible, is forged from the Arab-Islamic, Amazigh and Saharan-Hassani components, and enriched by the African, Andalusian, Hebraic and Mediterranean influences, as the preamble of its Constitution itself states. From the mellahs of Fez to the medinas of the north, from the Gnawa rhythms of Essaouira to the Hassani poetry of the south, this mosaic is not a juxtaposition of compartments but a set of crossed traditions, where each element has been transformed by the meeting of the others.",
