      en: "The Moroccan Sahara, a country of dunes and of regs, of nomadic tents and of oasis gardens, has its own culture, of which the Hassaniya dialect is the vehicle. Poetry of the desert, music of the tidinitt, cuisine of the camel and of the couscous of the south, and the great gatherings of the Tan-Tan Moussem: this Saharan-Hassani heritage, which Article 5 of the Constitution commits the State to preserve, is today carried by the cultural life of Laayoune, of Dakhla and of the provinces of the south.",
